WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.287
Here are all seven gates on one page.

2
00:00:02.287 --> 00:00:07.421
The first five are collection, one
per provider: Azure Service Health,

3
00:00:07.421 --> 00:00:12.825
Microsoft 365, Oracle Cloud Infrastructure,
AWS Health and Google Cloud.

4
00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:17.038
They're independent, so enable only
the providers the agency uses.

5
00:00:17.038 --> 00:00:21.812
Gate six routes what they collect: every
notice that needs action gets a task,

6
00:00:21.812 --> 00:00:24.388
and a second run doesn't
make a second task.

7
00:00:24.388 --> 00:00:26.762
Gate seven schedules the weekly run,

8
00:00:26.762 --> 00:00:31.275
sends the digest to the owners and
checks the evidence for each stage.

9
00:00:31.275 --> 00:00:34.825
Each gate is validated with
one of the kit's entry scripts.

10
00:00:34.825 --> 00:00:37.162
Every one of those checks only reads.

11
00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:39.862
The only writes are in
the kit's deploy folder,

12
00:00:39.862 --> 00:00:43.801
and they run only with an apply
switch and the plan's approved hash.

13
00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:48.380
And the checks are tested against
fixtures, not proven against a live tenant.
